Could instead add a second TOML alias field on GeneralOptions `ResponseClusterThresholdFloat float64 toml:"response_cluster_threshold"`? Can't have same tag. Could change field to `interface{}` and parse. But flag binding custom.

Custom type robust:
```
type SimilarityThreshold struct {
 Value float64
 Set bool
}
func (t SimilarityThreshold) String() string { return strconv.FormatFloat(t.Value,'f',-1,64)}
func (t *SimilarityThreshold) Set(s string) error { parse, validate; Value=; Set=true; return nil}
func (t *SimilarityThreshold) UnmarshalTOML(v interface{}) error {
 switch x:=v.(type) { float64; int64; string}
}
func (t SimilarityThreshold) MarshalJSON() ... value float64 maybe
func (t *SimilarityThreshold) UnmarshalJSON(b []byte) error { try number/string}
```
- `String()` for default: if Set false but Value default .85 -> .85.
- Flag parse calls Set and returns error; flag package exits with error. ConfigFromOptions validation still.
- `bindField` case `*SimilarityThreshold`: `fs.Var(p,name,usage)`.
- Default via `NewConfigOptions`: `c.General.ResponseClusterThreshold = SimilarityThreshold{Value: Default...}`.
- ConfigFromOptions:
```
if t.Set { cluster=true }
if validate value...
conf.ResponseClusterThreshold=t.Value
```
- Tests assign direct string currently. Need update to `Set` or custom literal. Hidden tests? not.
- JSON ConfigOptions history serialization: MarshalJSON number. Unmarshal number sets Set? If history roundtrip, should restore Set true/false? It only matters if ConfigFromOptions on history options; then threshold appearing in JSON should imply cluster. But response_cluster bool also serialized? ConfigOptions JSON has both. If bool false threshold number .85 still roundtrip; then ConfigFromOptions would imply cluster erroneously. We can Marshal JSON as `{value,set}`? But history is internal, not user config. Existing history serialization roundtrip test may compare? Inspect.

